# Feature-branch workflow

When the user asks for code or project changes in this repo, do not work on `master` (or `main`). This repo opts in to commit-and-push on feature branches without a separate "please commit" request.

## Before editing
1. If HEAD is `master`/`main`, create and check out a new branch named `cursor/<short-kebab-description>`.
2. If already on a feature branch that matches this request, keep using it.
3. Call SetActiveBranch after creating or switching branches.
4. Stage only files from this request. Leave unrelated dirty files (and secrets) unstaged.

## After the change is done
1. Commit the relevant files with a concise message focused on why.
2. Push the feature branch: `git push -u origin HEAD`.
3. Tell the user the branch name and that it is ready to test. Do not open a PR unless they ask.

## Never
- Do not `git push` to `master` or `main`.
- Do not merge into `master`/`main` until the user says they have tested and want it merged.
- Do not force-push, skip hooks, or amend unless the user explicitly asks.
